{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRODUCT CARD — SLIDER FACE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

One colour's worth of the slider card: image, kicker, title, rating, swatches, price and call to action. The colours of a
bed are separate products merged with the "my_fields.mcolors" metafield, the same list the product page reads, so a face
is simply that sibling product rendered in the card's own layout.

"product-card-slider" stacks one face per colour inside a single card and shows one at a time. Every face carries the
full swatch row with its own colour marked current, so switching face needs no state to be kept in sync: the incoming
face already shows the right swatch as selected.

********************************************
Supported variables
********************************************

* product: the product this face renders (required)
* swatch_products: the full list of colour siblings, used to draw the swatch row. Omit to hide the row
* active: true for the face shown first. Only the active face loads its image eagerly
* eager: if set to true, the active face's image loads eagerly. Only use on the first row of the page
* cta_text: the call to action label
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign card_kicker = product.metafields.custom.card_kicker.value | default: product.type
  assign cta_text = cta_text | default: 'Se sengen'

  comment
    Only the face on show is worth prioritising. The hidden faces stay lazy, so a card with four colours still costs one
    image on load — the browser holds off on a lazy image for as long as its face is display:none.
  endcomment
  if eager and active
    assign card_loading = 'eager'
    assign card_fetchpriority = 'high'
  else
    assign card_loading = 'lazy'
    assign card_fetchpriority = 'auto'
  endif

  assign color_label_list = 'general.label.color' | t | replace: ', ', ',' | downcase | split: ','
  assign color_option = nil

  comment
    This is a matching list, not copy: it holds the option names the theme recognises as a colour option.
    It stays as a locale lookup so a product using "Color" rather than "Farve" is still matched.
  endcomment
  for color_label in color_label_list
    if product.options_by_name[color_label] != blank
      assign color_option = product.options_by_name[color_label]
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Same label convention as product-card.liquid: a tag prefixed with __label: becomes the pill on the image.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture product_labels -%}
  {%- for tag in product.tags -%}
    {%- if tag contains '__label' -%}
      {{- tag | split: '__label:' | last -}}
      {%- break -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture sizes -%}
  (max-width: 699px) 78vw, (max-width: 999px) 52vw, 520px
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Sold out is a property of the colour, not of the card, so the modifier sits on the face. Its rule is written as a
  descendant selector, so it still finds the figure from here.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="story-card__face {% unless product.available %}story-card--unavailable{% endunless %}"
  data-color-face="{{ product.handle | escape }}"
  {% unless active %}hidden{% endunless %}
>
  {%- if product.media.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="story-card__figure">
      {%- render 'product-badges', product: product, vertical: true -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        The seals sit outside the media link, which is aria-hidden so the title carries the accessible name.
        Inside it the label text would be hidden from screen readers along with the rest of the link.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if product_labels != blank or product.metafields.custom.dansk_produceret_kvalitetsseng_ikon != blank -%}
        <div class="product-card--right-side">
          {%- if product_labels != blank -%}
            <div class="product-labels">
              <span class="product-label">{{ product_labels | strip }}</span>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if product.metafields.custom.dansk_produceret_kvalitetsseng_ikon != blank -%}
            <div class="product-card--right-side__icon">
              {%- render 'icon' with 'dansk-kvalitet' -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if product.metafields.custom.lagen_ikon != blank -%}
            <div class="product-card--right-side__icon2">
              {%- render 'icon' with 'lagen' -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <a href="{{ product.url }}" class="story-card__media" data-instant tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- capture image_classes -%}story-card__image zoom-image group-hover:zoom {% if settings.product_image_aspect_ratio contains 'crop' %}object-cover{% endif %}{%- endcapture -%}

        {{- product.featured_media
          | image_url: width: product.featured_media.width
          | image_tag:
            loading: card_loading,
            fetchpriority: card_fetchpriority,
            sizes: sizes,
            widths: '300,400,500,600,700,800,1000,1200,1400,1600',
            class: image_classes
        -}}

        {%- if settings.show_secondary_image and product.media.size > 1 -%}
          {%- assign next_media = product.media[product.featured_media.position] | default: product.media[1] -%}

          {{- next_media
            | image_url: width: next_media.width
            | image_tag:
              loading: 'lazy',
              fetchpriority: 'low',
              sizes: sizes,
              widths: '300,400,500,600,700,800,1000,1200,1400,1600',
              class: 'story-card__image story-card__image--secondary'
          -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      </a>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="story-card__content">
    <div class="v-stack gap-1">
      {%- if card_kicker != blank -%}
        <p class="smallcaps text-subdued">{{ card_kicker | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <a href="{{ product.url }}" class="story-card__title h5" data-instant>
        {%- if product.title contains ' | ' -%}
          {{- product.title | split: ' | ' | first | remove: ' -' -}}
        {%- else -%}
          {{- product.title -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="story-card__meta h-stack gap-2 wrap text-subdued">
      {%- comment -%}
        Reviews come from Yotpo, not from the native reviews.rating metafield that Prestige's product-rating
        snippet reads. Markup mirrors snippets/product-card.liquid, without its onclick handler, which scrolls
        to a product page tab that does not exist on a collection page.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <a class="story-card__reviews reviewLink" href="{{ product.url }}" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="yotpo yotpo-reviews bottomLine" data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"></div>
      </a>

      {%- comment -%}
        With merged colours the swatch row already says how many there are, so the count would repeat it. The count
        stays for beds whose colours are variants of one product rather than separate products.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if swatch_products == blank and color_option != blank and color_option.values.size > 1 -%}
        <p class="smallcaps">{{ color_option.values.size }} betræk</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if swatch_products != blank -%}
      <div class="story-card__swatches color-swatch-wrapper">
        {%- for swatch_product in swatch_products -%}
          {%- assign farve_object = swatch_product.metafields.custom.farve_filter.value -%}
          {%- assign is_current = false -%}
          {%- if swatch_product.handle == product.handle -%}
            {%- assign is_current = true -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            A button rather than the product page's link: the point here is to stay on the collection and swap the face.
            The product is still reachable through the title, the image and the call to action.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button
            type="button"
            class="story-card__swatch"
            data-color-target="{{ swatch_product.handle | escape }}"
            aria-pressed="{% if is_current %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
          >
            <span
              class="color-swatch {% if farve_object.farve_navn.value == 'Hvid' %}color-swatch-white{% endif %}"
              style="background-color: {{ farve_object.swatch.value }};"
            ></span>
            <span class="sr-only">{{ farve_object.farve_navn.value | default: swatch_product.title | escape }}</span>
          </button>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="story-card__footer v-stack gap-3">
      {%- if product.available -%}
        {%- render 'price-list', product: product, context: 'card', show_compare_at_text: true -%}

        {%- render 'button', href: product.url, content: cta_text, stretch: true -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <p class="h5 heading text-subdued">Udsolgt</p>

        {%- render 'button', href: product.url, content: cta_text, style: 'outline', stretch: true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
